::

The circled back button shows at ≤ 767px only — the two-plane contract (`messages.surf`, WP-N2): the thread replaces the roster rail full-width while `data-thread=open`, and `backToRoster` closes the state and returns to the rail; wide AND medium keep the roster beside the thread, so the back button never renders there. Presence dot: green, DMs only, only when online. Bubbles are authored via `::chat-thread` (v0.17) — `them` items = translucent glass left-aligned (bottom-left tightened), `own` items = accent fill right-aligned (bottom-right tightened), the `time=` timestamp in-bubble under each; group threads lead incoming bubbles with the `sender=` name, Surfy is a named sender with the accent lead; bubbles cap at min(75%, 640px). Reactions render as count pills under the bubble, "mine" state accent-tinted, optimistic toggle (`message_reacted` wire event). The attach ＋ is a plain gray circle (deliberately NOT accent). `@surfy` in the draft raises the accent hint bar "Surfy will reply in this thread" above the composer; Enter sends. No unread treatment renders inside a thread — and the accent-left-border unread idiom is BANNED everywhere regardless.

Compose mode (＋ New Conversation, no sheet): the thread pane flips to a **To:** line, autofocused — typing filters workspace members live, selection adds a recipient chip (✕ removes) with the cursor staying on the line; two-plus chips = a group; clicking the message input starts writing and the first send creates the conversation. The To: line is the `chip-input` kind:

::chip-input[label="To:" placeholder="Type a name…" source=members on-change="invoke:messages.compose"]
- Danny Pappageorge
::

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — shipped v0.17"]
Bubbles, timestamps, and sender leads now ride `::chat-thread` (SHIPPED v0.17) — the thread above authors dash-item messages (`them`/`own` with `sender=`/`time=`), replacing the old stand-in rows. The To:-line recipient chips ride the new `chip-input` kind (also v0.17): label, removable chips with the close glyph, inline filter input. Reaction pills shipped read-only this round ("mine" variant accent-tinted); presence stays a renderer treatment.
::

## Sheets and menus — defined once, opened from here

- **Attach menu** — `modals/attach-menu.surf`: an ANCHORED dropdown-select (RULED 08-05 — a menu, not a modal), via the composer ＋ (`openAttachMenu`). Document / Task / Photo.
- **Doc/Task attach picker** — `modals/doc-task-picker.surf` (`name=doc-task-picker`), one sheet, two modes — the title reads "Share a doc" / "Share a task" per the attach-menu row used (`openDocPicker` / `openTaskPicker`).
- **Media picker** — `modals/media-picker.surf` (`name=media-picker`), Surfspace image library first, OS Photo Library escape row (`openMediaPicker`).
- **Reaction palette + report** — `modals/react-report.surf` (`name=react-report`), anchored to the hovered bubble (`openReactReport`); six picks + the danger Report Message row (App Marketplace 1.2 UGC).
- **Participants** — `modals/participants.surf` (`name=participants`), via the header button (`openParticipants`). Read-only in v1.
